{"ref":"BDB, צֶ֫לֶם","hw":"צֶ֫לֶם","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">צֶ֫לֶם</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <sup><a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.17\">Ez 16:17</a></sup> <strong>image (</strong>something <em>cut out</em>, cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, פֶּ֫סֶל\" href=\"/BDB,_פֶּ֫סֶל\", dir=\"rtl\">פֶּסֶל</a>; Nö ‘Schnitzbild’<strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 39:7\" href=\"/Psalms.39.7\">ψ 39:7</a>, cstr. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 1:27\" href=\"/Genesis.1.27\">Gn 1:27</a> +; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">צַלְמוֹ</span> v <a data-ref=\"Genesis 1:27\" href=\"/Genesis.1.27\">27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 5:3\" href=\"/Genesis.5.3\">5:3</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">צַלְמֵנוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 1:26\" href=\"/Genesis.1.26\">1:26</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">צַלְמָם</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 73:20\" href=\"/Psalms.73.20\">ψ 73:20</a>; pl. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">צַלְמֵי</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:5\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.5\">1 S 6:5</a><sup>(×2)</sup> +, sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">צְלָמָיו</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 11:18\" href=\"/II_Kings.11.18\">2 K 11:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 23:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.23.17\">2 Ch 23:17</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">צַלְמֵיכֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"Amos 5:26\" href=\"/Amos.5.26\">Am 5:26</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>images</em> of tumours and mice (of gold) <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:5\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.5\">1 S 6:5</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:11\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.11\">11</a>; especially of heathen gods <a data-ref=\"Amos 5:26\" href=\"/Amos.5.26\">Am 5:26</a> (text dub.; del. We as gloss, cf. GASm Dr), <a data-ref=\"II Kings 11:18\" href=\"/II_Kings.11.18\">2 K 11:18</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 23:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.23.17\">2 Ch 23:17</a> (both c. vb. <span dir=\"rtl\">שִׁבְּרוּ</span>), <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 7:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.7.20\">Ez 7:20</a>, so <span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳ זָכָר</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.17\">16:17</a> (i.e. in male form, according to fig. of harlotry for idolatry); <span dir=\"rtl\">צַלְמֵי מַסֵּכֹתָם</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 33:52\" href=\"/Numbers.33.52\">Nu 33:52</a> <em>their molten images;</em> of painted pictures of men <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.14\">Ez 23:14</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>image, likeness</em>, of resemblance, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּצ׳ (בָּרָא) עָשָׂה</span>, of God’s making man in his own image, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 1:26\" href=\"/Genesis.1.26\">Gn 1:26</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">כִּדְמוּתֵנוּ</span>), v <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:27\" href=\"/Genesis.27.27\">27:27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 9:6\" href=\"/Genesis.9.6\">9:6</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּצ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 5:3\" href=\"/Genesis.5.3\">5:3</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">בִּדְמוּתוֹ</span>; all P).<br><strong>3.</strong>  fig. = <em>mere, empty, image, semblance</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּצ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 39:7\" href=\"/Psalms.39.7\">ψ 39:7</a> <em>as</em> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ב</span> essentiae) <em>a</em> (mere) <em>semblance man walks about;</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">צַלְמָם תִּבְזֶה</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 73:20\" href=\"/Psalms.73.20\">73:20</a> <em>thou wilt despise their semblance</em>.","next":"BDB, צַלְמוֹן","prev":"BDB, צלם"}